### Get Primitive

The get primitive will get a value from the source and save it in the target.

```text
get <from> ["keys"] <target>
```
Syntax Structure:
- `get`:
    * Type: *string*
    * This is the identifier for the instruction.
- `<from>` 
    * Type: *string*
    * This is the name of the participant whose value to get.
- `[keys]` 
    * Type: *Array*
    * This is an array of strings, representing the key path to key value to insert.
    * For example, ["a","b"] will be target_participant["a"]["b"]
    * If the key is specified as [], it indicates that the value should be directly assigned to the participant.
- `<target>` 
    * Type: *string*
    * This is the name of the participant the value will be saved in.

#### Example 1:
Inserts the book participant into the basket participant at index 0. It expects basket to be an array.

```text
get book ["name"] book_name
```

Pre-transformation state:
```text
    {
        book: {"name": "Lord of the Rings"},
        book_name: null,
    }
```

Post-transformation state:
```text
    {
        book: {"name": "Lord of the Rings"},
        book_name: "Lord of the Rings",
    }
```

#### Example 2:
Gets the value of book and saves it in book copy.

```text
get book [] book_copy
```

Pre-transformation state:
```text
    {
        book: {"name": "Lord of the Rings"},
        book_copy: null,
    }
```

Post-transformation state:
```text
    {
        book: {"name": "Lord of the Rings"},
        book_copy: {"name": "Lord of the Rings"},
    }
```